emove all counters from target permanent.","power":"2","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2020-08-07","toughness":"1","type_line":"Creature — Vampire Shaman"},{"cmc":4.0,"color_identity":[],"colors":[],"defense":null,"keywords":[],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"not_legal","paupercommander":"not_legal","penny":"legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"not_legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{4}","name":"Vedalken Orrery","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","oracle_text":"You may cast spells as though they had flash.","power":null,"produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2022-07-08","toughness":null,"type_line":"Artifact"},{"cmc":3.0,"color_identity":["W"],"colors":["W"],"defense":null,"keywords":["Flash"],"layout":"normal","legalities":{"alchemy":"not_legal","brawl":"not_legal","commander":"legal","competitivebrawl":"not_legal","duel":"legal","future":"not_legal","gladiator":"not_legal","historic":"not_legal","legacy":"legal","modern":"legal","oathbreaker":"legal","oldschool":"not_legal","pauper":"legal","paupercommander":"legal","penny":"not_legal","pioneer":"not_legal","predh":"not_legal","premodern":"not_legal","standard":"not_legal","standardbrawl":"not_legal","timeless":"not_legal","tlr":"legal","vintage":"legal"},"loyalty":null,"mana_cost":"{2}{W}","name":"Village Bell-Ringer","oracle_id":"d7b50175-b473-452a-bb30-19a71c42e649","oracle_text":"Flash (You may cast this spell any time you could cast an instant.)\nWhen this creature enters, untap all creatures you control.","power":"1","produced_mana":[],"released_at":"2023-04-21","toughness":"4","type_line":"Creature — Human Scout"}],"fixture_kind":"public_exact-list_card_data","rulings":[{"comment":"Gouged Zealot's triggered ability checks whether there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard to see if it triggers. If you don't, the ability won't trigger at all. The ability will check again as it tries to resolve. If you don't at that time, the ability won't do anything. The specific cards in your graveyard may change between the two checks.","oracle_id":"35b30274-bf8c-4d3c-b738-f9e62cdd5156","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The card types that can appear in a graveyard are artifact, battle, creature, enchantment, instant, kindred, land, planeswalker, and sorcery. Legendary, basic, and snow are supertypes, not card types; Cyclops and Berserker are subtypes, not card types.","oracle_id":"35b30274-bf8c-4d3c-b738-f9e62cdd5156","published_at":"2021-06-18","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of the enchanted creature, not the controller of Lifelink, gains the life (in case they’re different players).","oracle_id":"4fe8316a-9cff-43e9-a1d5-993a0c9daf3a","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The controller of Vedalken Orrery can cast nonland artifact, creature, enchantment, and sorcery cards any time they could cast an instant. This includes on other players' turns and during the upkeep step, draw step, combat phase, and end step.","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2004-12-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This applies only to casting spells. It does not, for example, change when you may activate abilities that can only be activated \"any time you could cast a sorcery\".","oracle_id":"60d640a4-032b-4279-ac75-8f200ca776fb","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Act of Treason can target any creature, even one that's untapped or one you already control.","oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Gaining control of a creature doesn't cause you to gain control of any Auras or Equipment attached to it.","oracle_id":"9d08af23-9f4a-4097-9abc-3b17475ab744","published_at":"2019-07-12","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If there are fewer than twenty cards in the targeted player's library, that player puts all the cards from their library into their graveyard.","oracle_id":"cc2b6e58-2d6f-495e-95f3-9496105c4cba","published_at":"2009-10-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"A creature’s level is based on how many level counters it has on it, not how many times its level up ability has been activated or has resolved. If a leveler gets level counters due to some other effect (such as Clockspinning) or loses level counters for some reason (such as Vampire Hexmage), its level is changed accordingly.","oracle_id":"d369a02b-c282-454a-9f89-480f4f5d838c","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Effects that modify a leveler’s power or toughness, such as the effects of Giant Growth or Glorious Anthem, will apply to it no matter when they started to take effect. The same is true for counters that change the creature’s power or toughness (such as +1/+1 counters) and effects that switch its power and toughness.","oracle_id":"d369a02b-c282-454a-9f89-480f4f5d838c","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Effects that set a leveler’s power or toughness to a specific value, including the effects from a level symbol’s ability, apply in timestamp order. The timestamp of each level symbol’s ability is the same as the timestamp of the leveler itself, regardless of when the most recent level counter was put on it.","oracle_id":"d369a02b-c282-454a-9f89-480f4f5d838c","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If another creature becomes a copy of a leveler, all of the leveler’s printed abilities — including those represented by level symbols — are copied. The current characteristics of the leveler, and the number of level counters on it, are not. The abilities, power, and toughness of the copy will be determined based on how many level counters are on the copy.","oracle_id":"d369a02b-c282-454a-9f89-480f4f5d838c","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In a multiplayer game, the only player affected by the last ability is the one Lord of Shatterskull Pass is attacking (or the one who controls the planeswalker Lord of Shatterskull Pass is attacking).","oracle_id":"d369a02b-c282-454a-9f89-480f4f5d838c","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The abilities a leveler grants to itself don’t overwrite any other abilities it may have. In particular, they don’t overwrite the creature’s level up ability; it always has that.","oracle_id":"d369a02b-c282-454a-9f89-480f4f5d838c","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"The last ability triggers and resolves during the declare attackers step, before blockers are declared.","oracle_id":"d369a02b-c282-454a-9f89-480f4f5d838c","published_at":"2010-06-15","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Untapping an attacking creature doesn't remove it from combat.","oracle_id":"d7b50175-b473-452a-bb30-19a71c42e649","published_at":"2011-09-22","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If a creature attacks a planeswalker, that planeswalker’s controller is the defending player.","oracle_id":"fc16a2ce-a570-454f-8498-f9c604c0d68b","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"In a Two-Headed Giant game, Swathcutter Giant deals 1 damage to each creature controlled by the player it’s attacking. The other player’s creatures are unaffected.","oracle_id":"fc16a2ce-a570-454f-8498-f9c604c0d68b","published_at":"2018-10-05","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Any permanent can be targeted by the second ability, not just one with counters on it.","oracle_id":"fcb2a95b-cef0-4b29-8b2b-538f380aff2b","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Vampire Hexmage's ability can't target a permanent card in a zone other than the battlefield, such as a suspended card.","oracle_id":"fcb2a95b-cef0-4b29-8b2b-538f380aff2b","published_at":"2021-03-19","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
